WEBVTT

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:19.320
A light so bright that it can't be hidden
Breaks the silence and resurrects in this world

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:30.070
The dry land quakes violently
Sparks clash as we risk our lives

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.810
Let a miracle occur, just one more time

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:44.950
The power to regain the pages of memories I lost long ago

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:53.020
The trusting heart pierces the darkness
Search for the place where the soul rests

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:59.250
The sharp glint in my unblinking eye burns

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:06.700
Two souls - light and shadow
To the future shown in the crystal

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:13.310
Now moving  Overflowing in red  eyes

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:36.470
The KC Grand Prix Tournament commemorates the opening of Kaiba Land USA.

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:41.380
It's exciting that duelists chosen from around the world are battling!

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:45.100
Jonouchi and Rebecca won their opening matches.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.520
They're in the Top 8.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:52.320
Their opponents will be stronger, but keep doing your best!

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:59.470
Jonouchi vs Sieg
Beautiful Duel

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:10.700
Here's the Top 8 in Kaiba Corporation's KC Grand Prix to crown the best duelist!

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:17.100
First, the undefeated young prodigy, Leon Wilson!

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:22.670
In this tournament, he’s winning with his careful dueling style.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:26.220
Facing this young prodigy...

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:32.910
The man-eating shark of the South Seas with his fierce fighting style: Ethan Shark!

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:39.720
Instead of standing around, I wanna duel!

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.810
Calm down, Jonouchi.

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:45.640
Everyone is using this time to rethink their strategies.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.660
You should take another look at your deck too.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:49.910
That’s right.

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:55.170
Your opponent is the guy that beat Ryuzaki and Haga in one turn.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:59.600
I beat them too!

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.530
And it's not my style to change last minute!

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:06.680
You're right.  Thinking won't help you, Jonouchi.

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:08.170
What?

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:12.210
Because your strengths are your instincts and luck.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:15.680
Hey!  You make it sound like I don’t think at all!

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.360
Is he wrong?

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.680
Why you!

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:19.870
You wanna fight?

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:21.300
Knock it off.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.170
You’re disturbing other people.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:23.820
Be quiet!

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.830
How dare you, Jonouchi!

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.470
Leon?

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.650
Jonouchi’s as relaxed as ever.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.690
But I’m nervous.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.890
What are you talking about?

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:39.630
You made the Top 8.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.700
Just be confident and be prepared for anything.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:48.960
But if I win, I get to duel my hero: Yugi.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.830
Just thinking that makes me nervous.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:55.580
So you're planning to win it all!

00:03:55.580 --> 00:04:00.620
Hold up.  If you win your next match, you'll face me in the semifinals.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:04.370
I won't give you the chance to duel my darling that easily.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:08.010
O-Okay.  Please go easy on me.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:12.890
No hard feelings, whoever wins.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.140
Thanks for waiting.  Go to standby.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:17.410
Okay, here I go!

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.860
Your name is Sieg, right?

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.180
Let’s have a good duel.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:31.040
Hey, wait up!

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:35.100
Show some courtesy to your next opponent!

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:41.520
Are you listening to me?

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.000
Don't touch me.

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:47.580
What?

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:48.510
Jonouchi!

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:53.280
I have no time for opponents who I’ll defeat easily.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:55.780
You don't know that!  We haven't dueled yet!

00:04:57.110 --> 00:05:01.200
The greatest fool is the one who doesn’t know his own power.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.050
You don’t even have a 1% chance of winning.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:08.750
Say what!  I made the Top 4 in Battle City!

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.050
Don’t underestimate me!

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:13.580
Then give it your best, no matter how pointless it is.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.070
You'll learn your place.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:17.500
You punk!

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.970
Knock it off, Jonouchi!

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:21.560
I won’t let him get away with that!

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:23.230
Let me go, Honda!

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:26.160
We’ll finish this in our duel!

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:28.210
Jonouchi…

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.210
Will Jonouchi be okay?

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:34.980
The duel hasn’t started, but his opponent is already in control.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:38.290
Darling, go cheer for Jonouchi.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:39.550
Rebecca…

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:43.220
I’ll be fine, but Jonouchi may be in trouble.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:45.980
Give him your support!

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:47.530
Are you sure?

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.460
You can root for me in my next match.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:55.920
But if Jonouchi ever faces me, you have to root for me, darling.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.740
Good luck, Rebecca!

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:02.650
All the support we were going to give Rebecca, let's give it to Jonouchi.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:05.990
Yeah.  Becky will be fine.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.880
Can I talk to you, Yugi?

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:11.160
Mokuba?

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:19.580
My brother told me to keep my eye on the competitors.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:21.500
What do you mean?

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:24.020
Before the tournament...

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:29.340
...remember how the computer malfunctioned and locked us inside the duel arena?

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:38.880
My brother thinks whoever hacked the computer will try something again.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:44.420
Our enemy is already here.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.740
You mean the hacker?

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:52.120
If you want to stop Kaiba Corporation’s comeback, have this tournament fail.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:56.690
But I’ve blocked outsiders from hacking in anymore.

00:06:56.690 --> 00:07:01.090
So whoever wants to cause trouble will have to sneak into this tournament.

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:05.100
I see.  Enter this tournament as one of the duelists.

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.080
The perpetrator will show up.

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:14.720
And when they do, I’ll crush them completely so they'll never threaten Kaiba Corporation again!

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:18.240
I’m running background checks on all the duelists.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:23.790
Mokuba, keep an eye out for any suspicious activities.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:30.700
I want your help because I can trust you.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:33.230
Let me know if you see anyone suspicious.

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:35.380
Suspicious, huh?

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:40.670
I think every duelist here is suspicious.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:42.990
What about them?

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:44.260
Them?

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:46.110
Ryuzaki and Haga.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:49.310
They snuck in here.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:51.820
It’s not them.

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:54.930
We sent them back to Japan already.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:01.930
No one comes to mind.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:03.890
You're right.

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:06.560
It’s sad.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:09.830
Yugi?

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:16.330
I thought everyone could have fun dueling, but someone's trying to wreck that.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:18.840
Partner...

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:25.110
Since they came from around the world, I want them to enjoy dueling.

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:26.740
Yugi…

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:31.130
Don’t worry!  I'll make sure this tournament is a success!

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:33.960
And we’ll help!

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:38.610
Let's keep an eye out for anyone suspicious and go cheer for Jonouchi!

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:39.910
Right, Yugi?

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:47.940
If we don't hurry, we’ll miss Jonouchi’s match!

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:49.940
Let's go!

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:53.080
The Top 8 will now collide!

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:57.630
Which of these eight will be victorious?

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.570
Journey to the center of the earth.

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:48.260
I’ve seen this attraction before.

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:49.730
There he is!

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.650
We’re here to cheer you on, Jonouchi!

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:55.090
Good luck!

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:56.740
Leave it to me!

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:11.490
I’ll make you regret what you said.

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:26.200
What are you looking at?

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:27.870
Don't ignore me!

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.080
Well?

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:36.520
Will Jonouchi be okay?

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:39.010
Don’t lose your cool, Jonouchi!

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:40.490
Relax!

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.500
I refuse to lose to you!

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:49.720
Bring it on, fool.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.460
Start the duel!

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:06.910
Duel!

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:30.740
He's so patronizing.

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.030
He's just like Kaiba!

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:34.600
Jonouchi, stay calm!

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:35.680
Keep cool!

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:38.680
I’ll show him my skills!

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:41.050
I go first!  I draw!

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:42.500
Here I go-

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:46.600
What's wrong with Jonouchi?

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:47.830
Jonouchi?

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:50.330
Oh no!

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:53.560
I don't have a monster card I can summon!

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:54.850
What’s wrong?

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:58.100
I thought you were going to show me your skills.

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:03.100
I set one card and end my turn!

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:05.030
Just a set card?

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:07.480
He must've had no monsters in his hand.

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:09.100
Jonouchi!

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.370
My turn.  I draw.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.640
Here it comes!

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:16.650
I activate a spell card from my hand.

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:18.150
Graceful Charity.

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:23.020
It lets me draw three cards from my deck and discard two.

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:27.030
I set one card and end my turn.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:33.300
He didn’t draw a monster card either?

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:36.070
Nice!  You’re in luck, Jonouchi!

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:38.400
Partner…

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:43.580
My other self, does he really not have any monster cards?

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:48.660
Something's up.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:55.780
Ha!  You had no monsters to summon either!

00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:58.440
After all your trash talk?

00:12:58.440 --> 00:13:00.340
You make me laugh!

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:05.500
Are you watching, Kaiba?

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:11.870
I know you’re desperately trying to uncover my identity, but I'm getting bored.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:15.380
I’ll give you a small hint.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.150
It’s time!

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:25.690
Okay, my turn!  I draw!

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.780
What?

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:36.420
These special effects are incredible!

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:39.960
That’s weird.  None of this is supposed to happen.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.670
Really?

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:47.750
This tournament is broadcast worldwide to promote Kaiba Land's opening, right?

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:50.450
Maybe that's why you have lots of effects.

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:58.180
My turn!  I draw!

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:02.430
Marco, what should I play next?

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:07.200
That one?  Good boy!

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:13.830
What?

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:19.100
I activate a spell card from my hand.

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:26.640
What's going on?

00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:38.980
I knew they'd try something!

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:41.800
Master Seto, the attractions are malfunctioning!

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:42.920
I know!

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:48.130
But I've severed all outside access!

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:56.440
When they hacked in earlier, they set a virus time bomb.

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:59.800
Who can do this without me noticing...

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:03.980
Was it that arrogant girl?

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:06.120
No, that's unlikely.

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:09.980
But not many people can do this.

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:14.120
For me, it’s a cinch.

00:15:23.780 --> 00:15:26.330
Thank you for the invitation.

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:31.340
Mr. Kaiba, you chose a worthy successor.

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:34.350
But he's pretty good too.

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:36.350
He’s a genius.

00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:39.850
I can see this party bores you.

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:42.320
Shall I make it entertaining?

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:48.070
What's going on?

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:49.960
Master Gozaburo.

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:53.120
A computer virus?

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.240
Impossible!

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:58.240
The main computer has high-security protection.

00:15:58.240 --> 00:15:59.910
Who could do this?

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:04.540
For me, it’s a cinch.

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:07.570
Actually, you can do it too.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:09.910
They call us both geniuses.

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:11.880
Let's be friends.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.420
Can it be?

00:16:14.420 --> 00:16:17.680
No, that was long ago.

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:25.990
These special effects will put me in the spotlight!

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:27.760
Here I go!

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:31.670
I summon Brigadier of Landstar in attack position!

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:39.540
Then I activate the Equip Spell, Landstar Shot from my hand!

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:46.850
It's an Equip Spell specially made for Brigadier of Landstar!

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:49.420
It gains 600 attack points!

00:16:51.130 --> 00:16:53.160
Go, Brigadier of Landstar!

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:55.110
Attack him directly!

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:59.300
I activate my trap card, Wotan's Judgment.

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:05.060
This trap activates when your monster attacks.

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:12.000
It swaps a spell card in my hand with the top card in my deck, and then I shuffle.

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:19.430
And it negates your monster’s attack and ends the Battle Phase.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:23.850
So close!  It was his chance!

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:32.760
He didn't use that trap just to end the Battle Phase.

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:37.870
Yeah.  He's planning to do something by getting new cards.

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:44.460
I can see why he was chosen to compete.

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:46.640
I end my turn!

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:49.280
My turn.  I draw.

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:53.040
I activate my spell card, Pot of Greed.

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:56.820
I draw two new cards.

00:17:58.020 --> 00:18:00.180
I activate another spell card.

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.440
Goddess Erda's Guidance.

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:08.960
Erda - the goddess of earth and knowledge - sees the past, present, and future.

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:10.830
The hand is the future.

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:12.600
The field is the present.

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:14.100
The graveyard is the past.

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:22.720
By sending a spell card in my hand to the graveyard...

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:27.380
...this card lets me get a trap card from my graveyard and set it.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:34.390
If that’s a trap card, it must be the one he just used: Wotan's Judgment.

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:36.390
I end my turn.

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:37.400
What?

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:39.840
He didn't summon a monster?

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:42.800
So he still doesn't have a monster in his hand?

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:44.320
That’s impossible!

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:48.680
He’s waiting for a specific card.

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:55.310
If Jonouchi attacks next turn, he can use Wotan's Judgment to draw a card again.

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:59.090
Is it the card he used to defeat Haga and Ryuzaki?

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:07.850
Seems you're having trouble, Kaiba.

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:13.130
If you can’t fix this, I must've overestimated you.

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:14.890
Hey you!

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:18.530
What are you always looking at?

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:20.170
Face me!

00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:24.670
You're so confident that you don’t have to pay attention?

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:26.480
Focus on the duel!

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:30.170
I don't need to use all my strength against you.

00:19:30.170 --> 00:19:34.210
You’re just a clown I need to duel before I move on.

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:35.950
Clown?

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:40.220
So be a good clown and keep dancing like a fool.

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:41.720
What’s with this guy!

00:19:42.970 --> 00:19:45.720
Trying to provoke me?  It won't work!

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:48.730
If you underestimate me, you’ll regret it!

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:50.230
My turn!

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:51.760
I draw!

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:54.460
I tribute Brigadier of Landstar!

00:19:56.670 --> 00:20:00.360
I summon Jinzo in attack position!

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:05.900
Jinzo’s effect activates!

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:07.880
All traps are negated!

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:09.880
Trap Search!

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:13.780
What?

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:17.140
Then Jinzo attacks you directly!

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:19.860
Cyber Energy Shock!

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:25.640
That wake you up?

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:30.890
You're facing a real duelist!  Katsuya Jonouchi!

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:35.480
He did it!

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:38.660
Keep pummeling him!

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:40.480
I end my turn.

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:42.110
Now bring it for real!

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:46.210
You did what you shouldn't have done.

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:49.880
And for that, you will be punished!  You fool!

00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:55.480
It's too late to regret making me serious.

00:20:56.530 --> 00:20:58.920
My turn.  I draw!

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:06.070
I'll show you the beautiful female warriors from Valhalla!

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:07.850
It's that card!

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:08.850
I knew it!

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:13.850
I activate my spell card, Ride of the Valkyries!

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:13.830
Right now, we don't need a map

00:22:13.990 --> 00:22:29.550
The miracle that tore through the darkness is in my hand

00:22:30.270 --> 00:22:35.390
Without a goal in mind

00:22:36.710 --> 00:22:43.960
We just step towards our dream

00:22:44.350 --> 00:22:49.600
EYE'S  As you sense it

00:22:49.790 --> 00:22:58.070
Your eye will find it

00:22:58.430 --> 00:23:03.880
Oh! EYE'S  What you wish for

00:23:04.670 --> 00:23:12.020
Will touch your soul

00:23:12.210 --> 00:23:15.280
In a duel

00:23:26.350 --> 00:23:33.230
Is the person Mokuba said is trying to ruin the tournament here in this arena?

00:23:33.230 --> 00:23:37.310
Is that person causing the attractions to malfunction?

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:41.760
That is concerning, but I have to focus on cheering for Jonouchi.

00:23:41.760 --> 00:23:45.700
That arrogant Sieg drew a card.

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:49.770
Is it the one that defeated Haga and Ryuzaki instantly?

00:23:49.770 --> 00:23:52.480
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Goddess of Monster Destruction

00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:54.110
Duel, standby!
